WEBVTT

00:04.142 --> 00:07.441
&lt;i>Oh, the weather outside is frightful&lt;/i>

00:07.612 --> 00:10.706
&lt;i>But the fire is so delightful&lt;/i>

00:10.915 --> 00:13.509
&lt;i>And since we've no place to go&lt;/i>

00:13.685 --> 00:17.177
&lt;i>Let it snow, let it snow, let it snow&lt;/i>

00:18.189 --> 00:23.149
Snow, sleet, rain, sun,
you've still got no place to go.

00:24.029 --> 00:27.760
Which is why I'm
grateful for your generosity, Mr. Scrooge.

00:29.634 --> 00:33.468
Speaking of generosity,
check out what I got Chelsea.

00:33.638 --> 00:35.105
Diamond earrings. Nice.

00:35.273 --> 00:38.504
Yeah. She dropped a couple of hints
about stuff she wanted.

00:38.676 --> 00:41.042
But I wasn't really listening,
so I got her these.

00:41.212 --> 00:43.510
How romantic.
Will she be joining us for dinner?

00:43.681 --> 00:46.582
I think so. She's out
doing some last-minute shopping...

00:46.751 --> 00:50.084
...or something with work.
Again, I wasn't really listening.

00:51.222 --> 00:52.689
Why did you mail me a letter?

00:52.857 --> 00:55.587
Oh, I decided to send out
a Harper Christmas newsletter.

00:55.760 --> 00:58.752
You know, keep everybody updated
on all things Harper.

00:58.963 --> 01:00.931
- You're kidding.
- Don't worry, governor.

01:01.099 --> 01:05.092
I didn't mention your ongoing battle
with the demon rum.

01:11.042 --> 01:13.670
&lt;i>As this wonderful year
Draws to an end&lt;/i>

01:13.845 --> 01:16.439
&lt;i>I send this note
To family and friend&lt;/i>

01:16.614 --> 01:19.208
&lt;i>So thankful are we
For blessings galore&lt;/i>

01:19.384 --> 01:23.616
&lt;i>Like Charlie's fiancée
A lady, not a whore&lt;/i>

01:24.889 --> 01:26.754
Keep reading.

01:27.992 --> 01:30.256
&lt;i>And young Master Jake
Is growing like a weed&lt;/i>

01:30.428 --> 01:34.421
&lt;i>He makes us all proud
Not a waste of my seed&lt;/i>

01:35.233 --> 01:36.723
Keep going. Keep going.

01:36.901 --> 01:38.869
&lt;i>He tried his darnedest
In every class&lt;/i>

01:39.037 --> 01:41.562
&lt;i>And made 10th grade
By the skin of his ass&lt;/i>

01:41.739 --> 01:45.698
And, see, I put in a little drawing
of an elf with his pants down.

01:45.877 --> 01:48.107
What's the matter with you?
You're a grown man.

01:48.279 --> 01:51.442
Oh, come on, people love this stuff.
Read, read.

01:51.616 --> 01:54.312
&lt;i>And our sweet mother, Evelyn
Had a small operation&lt;/i>

01:54.519 --> 01:58.546
&lt;i>Her secret garden
Needed rejuvenation&lt;/i>

01:59.257 --> 02:03.557
- "Secret garden"?
- Find a rhyme for "vulva."

02:03.728 --> 02:05.525
I dare you.

02:06.431 --> 02:08.763
&lt;i>And what about the author
Of this Christmas poem?&lt;/i>

02:08.933 --> 02:11.333
&lt;i>He's healthy and happy
In his beautiful home&lt;/i>

02:11.536 --> 02:13.936
&lt;i>And while some might argue
That he's just a leech&lt;/i>

02:14.105 --> 02:16.471
&lt;i>It bothers him not
He lives at the beach&lt;/i>

02:19.177 --> 02:21.441
"Happy holidays
from the happy Harpers."

02:21.613 --> 02:23.604
What do you think?

02:23.781 --> 02:26.443
&lt;i>You're sad, pathetic
Lonely and blue&lt;/i>

02:26.618 --> 02:29.280
&lt;i>If I gave a rat's ass
I'd worry about you&lt;/i>

02:41.499 --> 02:44.468
Expecting rough weather, captain?

02:45.136 --> 02:46.831
What?

02:47.639 --> 02:49.334
What are you looking at?

02:49.507 --> 02:51.600
- Nothing.
- Really?

02:51.776 --> 02:55.303
So the beautiful girls playing volleyball
completely escaped your eye?

02:55.480 --> 02:57.880
I see them, you perv.

02:59.317 --> 03:02.047
Little hottie in the tank top
is checking you out.

03:02.220 --> 03:05.383
I know. Now, please go away.

03:07.192 --> 03:08.625
Why don't you go talk to her?

03:08.793 --> 03:10.658
- I can't.
- Well, why not?

03:10.828 --> 03:12.125
I got a girlfriend.

03:12.297 --> 03:16.324
Oh, buddy, you can't call the posters
in your room girlfriends.

03:16.501 --> 03:19.493
No, I'm talking about Celeste.
I'm in a committed relationship.

03:19.671 --> 03:23.004
- What are you talking about? You're 13.
- I'm 15.

03:24.008 --> 03:27.466
Who cares? You're too young
for a committed relationship.

03:27.645 --> 03:30.705
- I'm 40, and I'm barely ready.
- You're 42.

03:30.882 --> 03:33.544
What is it with you and numbers?

03:34.319 --> 03:37.254
Let me ask you something.
Where is Celeste right now?

03:37.422 --> 03:39.617
Spending Christmas
with her mom in Brentwood.

03:39.791 --> 03:42.191
So, what, your life just stops
when she's gone?

03:42.360 --> 03:44.225
That's the deal we made.

03:45.363 --> 03:47.991
Listen to me,
if you wanna go talk to the beach girl...

03:48.166 --> 03:49.929
...you've got every right to do so.

03:50.134 --> 03:53.626
Are you sure? I don't think so.

03:54.772 --> 03:56.763
Don't worry about it.
Just go talk to her.

03:57.175 --> 03:59.234
- Can I borrow 10 bucks?
- Why?

03:59.410 --> 04:02.277
If she shoots me down,
then I can go buy a couple corn dogs.

04:02.447 --> 04:04.381
She's not gonna shoot you down.

04:04.549 --> 04:06.608
Yeah, but now I got a taste
for corn dogs.

04:06.784 --> 04:09.048
- Just go.
- What if she wants a corn dog?

04:09.220 --> 04:12.280
She's about to meet one.
Now, get out of here.

04:14.225 --> 04:15.749
Do I look okay?

04:15.927 --> 04:20.728
Jake, she waved at you. She smiled.
Clearly, her standards aren't that high.

04:22.166 --> 04:23.394
Right. Thanks.

04:27.572 --> 04:30.473
When did I turn 42?

04:32.176 --> 04:35.077
Son of a bitch.

04:35.246 --> 04:38.306
Hey, I'm an organ donor.
Good for me.

05:08.946 --> 05:13.576
- Hey, Berta. Merry Christmas.
- Thank you, Charlie.

05:13.751 --> 05:16.413
- You're very generous.
- Well, I just want you to know...

05:16.587 --> 05:18.452
...that I appreciate your hard work.

05:18.623 --> 05:21.751
And I appreciate
you pretending I work hard.

05:22.827 --> 05:26.285
- Hey, you feeling lucky?
- What do you got in mind?

05:26.464 --> 05:30.400
My Christmas bonus, double or nothing
that Zrbnck makes the field goal.

05:30.768 --> 05:34.101
Are you crazy? That's 52 yards.
He hasn't made one that long all year.

05:34.272 --> 05:37.241
- I got a hunch.
- And you got a bet.

05:37.408 --> 05:40.639
&lt;i>There's the snap.
The kick is up. It's long enough, but wide.&lt;/i>

05:40.845 --> 05:44.975
&lt;i>It's no good.
Zrbnck's missed another one.&lt;/i>

05:45.149 --> 05:47.982
Well, happy birthday, Jesus.

05:51.622 --> 05:56.059
- Told you.
- No biggie. Easy come, easy go.

05:56.394 --> 05:57.452
Sorry.

05:57.628 --> 06:01.587
Looks like the grandkids are getting
beef jerky and lotto scratchers this year.

06:05.136 --> 06:06.626
Here.

06:06.804 --> 06:09.068
- You're too kind.
- Don't mention it.

06:09.240 --> 06:12.175
- You got a big heart.
- Thank you.

06:12.377 --> 06:15.471
Double or nothing
they don't make first down.

06:16.781 --> 06:18.681
- Hey.
- Oh, hey. Where you been?

06:18.850 --> 06:20.317
- Out on the beach.
So?

06:20.485 --> 06:22.976
- How'd it go?
Fine. I'm getting her a grape soda.

06:23.154 --> 06:25.520
No, no, no,
you don't bring the grape soda to her.

06:25.690 --> 06:28.158
- You bring her to the grape soda.
- Her who?

06:28.326 --> 06:32.126
Hang on. You bring her here,
she sees your beautiful house...

06:32.296 --> 06:35.959
...she thinks you got it going on,
and then you got a shot at...

06:37.535 --> 06:40.834
Well, I don't know what
you got a shot at, but you got a shot.

06:41.005 --> 06:43.530
- Whoa, whoa, catch me up.
- You see what I'm saying?

06:43.708 --> 06:46.199
- So I should bring her here?
- Absolutely.

06:46.411 --> 06:49.039
Women love this house.
It's an aphrodisiac.

06:49.213 --> 06:51.909
I don't think she's Afro-anything.

06:53.684 --> 06:57.211
- She's more like Chinese.
- Wait. Who's Chinese? What's going on?

06:57.388 --> 07:00.323
- He met a girl, and I'm helping him out.
- What about Celeste?

07:00.491 --> 07:03.949
Uncle Charlie said my life shouldn't stop
just because she's not around.

07:04.128 --> 07:06.790
So you're encouraging my son
to cheat on his girlfriend?

07:06.964 --> 07:09.398
There's no cheating going on.
Are you cheating?

07:09.567 --> 07:11.125
- I'm not sure.
- You're not.

07:11.302 --> 07:15.238
He is. How would you feel if Celeste
was flirting with some other guy?

07:15.406 --> 07:17.704
- How do you know she's not?
- She's with her mom.

07:17.875 --> 07:21.333
And you're with your dad,
but that's not stopping you, is it?

07:21.846 --> 07:24.406
- Good point.
- No, no, it's a lousy point.

07:24.582 --> 07:27.380
Relationships are built on trust
and mutual respect.

07:27.552 --> 07:31.818
Oh, grow up. Relationships are built
on diamond earrings and Viagra.

07:33.591 --> 07:35.684
Now, go take the young lady
her grape soda.

07:35.860 --> 07:39.557
I still think it would help if I had
some corn-dog money to flash around.

07:39.730 --> 07:41.357
Go.

07:43.201 --> 07:45.226
- Shame on you.
- Well, what's the big deal?

07:45.403 --> 07:47.871
It's not like he and Celeste
are sleeping together.

07:48.039 --> 07:50.735
No, but once a relationship reaches
any physical level...

07:50.908 --> 07:53.035
...there's an implied commitment.
- Yeah.

07:53.211 --> 07:56.772
That's because you married
the first girl who touched your wiener.

07:57.348 --> 07:58.508
Not true.

07:58.683 --> 08:01.584
The first girl who touched my wiener
was Maxine Chernakoff...

08:01.752 --> 08:04.550
...and she refused to marry me.

08:07.391 --> 08:10.690
As did the blind girl at camp,
the school nurse...

08:10.862 --> 08:13.626
...and crazy cousin Wendy.

08:19.437 --> 08:21.769
I hope you're proud of yourself.

08:21.939 --> 08:24.931
I'm more proud of him.
I mean, he actually got her back here...

08:25.109 --> 08:28.806
...without hitting her over the head
and stuffing her in a burlap sack.

08:30.515 --> 08:32.574
Pretty girl.
- Yep.

08:32.750 --> 08:35.583
You'd think she'd have
more self-esteem.

08:36.320 --> 08:37.912
Hey, Jake may be dull-witted...

08:38.089 --> 08:40.785
&lt;i>...but he has a certain
je ne sais quoi with the ladies.&lt;/i>

08:40.958 --> 08:44.121
Maybe six years of picking his
underwear up with a rake...

08:44.295 --> 08:46.286
...has made me immune
to his charms.

08:49.400 --> 08:50.458
- Hey.
- Hey.

08:50.635 --> 08:52.967
Nice work
talking her into coming back here.

08:53.137 --> 08:56.004
I didn't really talk her into it.
She had to pee.

08:56.173 --> 09:00.109
Yeah, but you gave her the grape soda
that made it happen.

09:00.278 --> 09:03.770
Now, Jake, you're just hanging out
with this girl, right? As friends?

09:03.948 --> 09:05.575
- So far.
- What does that mean?

09:05.750 --> 09:07.945
It means I haven't made my move yet.

09:08.119 --> 09:10.019
- What move?
- I'm not sure.

09:10.187 --> 09:14.317
That's why I haven't made it yet.
I don't think it's gonna get serious.

09:14.492 --> 09:16.790
- She doesn't even live here.
- She doesn't?

09:16.961 --> 09:19.293
She's in town for the holidays
visiting her aunt.

09:19.463 --> 09:22.193
She pronounced it "aunt,"
but I figured it out.

09:22.366 --> 09:25.597
Oh, dude,
you have hit the jackpot here.

09:25.770 --> 09:27.704
- I have?
- This girl is most likely...

09:27.872 --> 09:30.602
...looking for a hot story
to tell her friends back home.

09:30.775 --> 09:35.371
And you, you cute little clueless
bastard, can be the star of that story.

09:35.546 --> 09:37.104
- Really?
- Yeah.

09:37.281 --> 09:39.613
So stop wasting time.
What are you doing in here?

09:39.784 --> 09:42.776
I had to fart,
and I didn't wanna do it in front of her.

09:43.955 --> 09:46.116
Attaboy. Good thinking.

09:46.490 --> 09:48.685
- I thought it was you.
- I thought it was you.

09:50.728 --> 09:51.888
Oh, that must be Mom.

09:52.063 --> 09:55.191
- Mom? What's Mom doing here?
- Well, it's Christmas Eve, Charlie.

09:55.366 --> 09:58.460
I know. Why isn't she out
stealing toys in Whoville?

10:01.505 --> 10:03.973
Merry Christmas, one and all.

10:04.141 --> 10:05.574
Oh, hello.
- Hi, Mom.

10:05.743 --> 10:10.373
Boys, this is legendary TV producer
Mr. Marty Pepper.

10:10.548 --> 10:11.674
- Hi.
- Hello.

10:11.849 --> 10:15.580
Marty, these are my sons,
Charlie and Alan.

10:15.753 --> 10:18.551
Is it important which is which?

10:19.523 --> 10:20.990
Not really.

10:21.158 --> 10:23.524
Would you help me
with the wheelchair?

10:23.694 --> 10:29.564
I'll call you Scooter, and you Dutch.

10:31.569 --> 10:35.562
- Mom, are you and he?
- Oh, good Lord, no.

10:35.740 --> 10:37.867
The man is 1000 years old.

10:38.042 --> 10:41.068
It's a wonder his scrotum
doesn't get tangled up in the wheels.

10:42.647 --> 10:44.877
- So he's just a friend?
- Yes.

10:45.049 --> 10:48.246
And I just couldn't let him spend
Christmas Eve alone...

10:48.419 --> 10:51.582
...rattling around his 25,000-square-foot
Beverly Hills mansion...

10:51.756 --> 10:54.623
...with adjoining guesthouse,
Olympic-size saltwater pool...

10:54.792 --> 10:56.123
...and home theater.

10:56.293 --> 11:00.354
- There it is.
- Are you really this hard up for a listing?

11:01.198 --> 11:06.431
Alan, it's a 60-million-dollar home.
My commission will be almost 2 million.

11:06.604 --> 11:08.401
How much did you make last year?

11:09.807 --> 11:14.437
- Welcome to our home, Mr. Pepper.
- What are you shouting for?

11:14.612 --> 11:18.070
- I'm incontinent, not deaf.
- Sorry.

11:18.249 --> 11:19.443
What?

11:21.218 --> 11:24.881
- Have an Abba-Zaba, Marty.
- Thank you.

11:25.056 --> 11:29.755
- Did I ever tell you I knew Lucille Ball?
- Yes, you did, dear.

11:29.927 --> 11:32.725
You know, she wasn't a real redhead.

11:32.897 --> 11:35.229
Ask me how I know.

11:35.399 --> 11:37.890
Warning: It's dirty.

11:39.203 --> 11:41.728
I think Celeste knows
I'm seeing another woman.

11:41.906 --> 11:44.067
- What? Why?
- She's texting me.

11:44.241 --> 11:46.106
- What are you talking about?
- Nothing.

11:46.277 --> 11:48.404
Jake has a shot
at some out-of-town strange.

11:48.579 --> 11:50.672
You see how he is corrupting
your grandson?

11:50.848 --> 11:53.976
Oh, come on, Alan,
it's out-of-town strange.

11:56.087 --> 11:57.918
- You really have a shot?
- I don't know.

11:58.089 --> 11:59.647
Uncle Charlie seems to think so.

11:59.824 --> 12:04.158
Tell her you wanna get her
her own sitcom. Never fails.

12:05.763 --> 12:07.355
There she is again. What do I do?

12:07.531 --> 12:11.160
Just text her back, "Thinking of you,"
which you are, so you're not lying.

12:11.335 --> 12:13.303
- That's good.
- This may be your house...

12:13.471 --> 12:16.463
...but this is my son.
- You've been living here seven years...

12:16.640 --> 12:20.007
...which makes us a common-law
couple, which makes him our son.

12:21.145 --> 12:25.275
Homos with a kid!
A great idea for a sitcom.

12:27.151 --> 12:29.813
It worked. She wrote back,
"Merry Christmas. I miz you."

12:29.987 --> 12:34.856
- Then write back, "I miz you too."
- Man, you are good.

12:36.994 --> 12:40.361
Look at that.
Our little boy is growing up.

12:40.531 --> 12:43.557
How would you feel
about us having another child?

12:51.275 --> 12:53.937
&lt;i>Jingle bell, jingle bell, jingle bell rock&lt;/i>

12:54.845 --> 12:57.837
&lt;i>Jingle bells swing and jingle bells ring&lt;/i>

12:58.382 --> 13:01.351
&lt;i>Snowing and blowing up bushels of fun&lt;/i>

13:02.253 --> 13:05.154
&lt;i>Now the jingle hop has begun&lt;/i>

13:05.556 --> 13:08.491
&lt;i>Jingle bell, jingle bell, jingle bell rock&lt;/i>

13:09.160 --> 13:12.357
&lt;i>Jingle bells chime in jingle bell time&lt;/i>

13:12.730 --> 13:16.029
&lt;i>Dancing and prancing in Jingle Bell Square&lt;/i>

13:16.700 --> 13:18.964
&lt;i>In the frosty air&lt;/i>

13:19.303 --> 13:22.739
&lt;i>What a bright time, it's the right time&lt;/i>

13:22.907 --> 13:25.239
&lt;i>To rock the night away&lt;/i>

13:26.577 --> 13:29.910
&lt;i>Jingle bell time is a swell time&lt;/i>

13:30.781 --> 13:33.773
&lt;i>To go gliding in a one-horse sleigh&lt;/i>

13:33.951 --> 13:36.920
&lt;i>Giddy-up jingle horse, pick up your feet&lt;/i>

13:37.288 --> 13:39.313
&lt;i>Jingle around the clock&lt;/i>

13:39.657 --> 13:43.320
&lt;i>- Alan.
- Mix and mingle with the jingling feet&lt;/i>

13:43.594 --> 13:45.858
&lt;i>- Alan.
- That's the jingle bell&lt;/i>

13:46.464 --> 13:50.366
&lt;i>- That's the jingle bell...
- Alan!&lt;/i>

14:00.444 --> 14:03.641
Forty years ago, you asked
for a little brother for Christmas.

14:04.114 --> 14:06.014
Happy?

14:07.284 --> 14:10.879
&lt;i>That's the jingle bell rock!&lt;/i>

14:16.293 --> 14:17.760
Can somebody move me?

14:17.928 --> 14:21.489
My chestnuts are roasting
by this open fire.

14:22.633 --> 14:26.626
Is that you?
I thought Alan burned the ham.

14:30.341 --> 14:33.538
Berta, don't you wanna spend
Christmas with your family?

14:33.711 --> 14:36.009
Do you wanna spend Christmas
with yours?

14:37.114 --> 14:38.376
Let me freshen your drink.

14:40.718 --> 14:43.846
What is that fragrance you're wearing,
my dear?

14:44.321 --> 14:46.346
Ben-Gay and foot powder.

14:47.791 --> 14:51.386
Whatever it is, it's making me hot.

14:52.196 --> 14:55.461
Turkey's almost done. Aren't you
gonna put on some nice clothes?

14:55.633 --> 14:59.160
Why? It's just gonna be you, me,
Chelsea, Berta, Mom...

14:59.336 --> 15:01.600
...and the Ghost of Show Biz Past.

15:01.772 --> 15:02.864
Well, and Jake.

15:03.040 --> 15:05.235
- No. Jake split.
- What?

15:05.409 --> 15:08.003
- He's hanging with his new girlfriend.
- Where?

15:08.178 --> 15:11.113
Her aunt's house. I think
they got the place to themselves...

15:11.282 --> 15:14.718
...so he might get a little, you know,
peace on earth tonight.

15:15.386 --> 15:17.854
How do you make everything
sound dirty?

15:18.022 --> 15:19.284
Hey, I took the high road.

15:19.456 --> 15:22.653
I could've gone with,
"Come, all ye faithful."

15:24.895 --> 15:26.863
- He needs to be home.
- Oh, come on, Alan.

15:27.031 --> 15:29.932
- He's got a real shot with that girl.
- It's Christmas Eve.

15:30.100 --> 15:33.467
- So?
- So if I can't get laid, nobody gets laid.

15:34.038 --> 15:37.804
This is your father. Whatever you're
doing, stop it and get your ass home.

15:37.975 --> 15:40.910
- What's he doing? Decking her hall?
- Shut up.

15:42.346 --> 15:44.814
No, right now, mister.

15:45.416 --> 15:48.408
Fine, bring her back here if you want.

15:48.619 --> 15:50.246
Yes, there's still pie left.

15:54.425 --> 15:55.915
What are you looking at?

16:01.131 --> 16:04.589
How would you like
to have your own sitcom?

16:05.536 --> 16:08.835
- Hi. Is Jake home?
I don't know.

16:09.006 --> 16:12.498
Sorry to intrude, but Celeste wanted
to give Jake his Christmas present.

16:12.676 --> 16:15.144
Please come in.
- Ah, crap.

16:16.046 --> 16:18.378
Wow, check out the mom.

16:18.549 --> 16:21.177
Forget the mom.
Get rid of them before Jake walks in...

16:21.352 --> 16:23.513
...with another girl.
- Yeah, yeah. Good idea.

16:23.687 --> 16:27.282
Hi. Hi.
I'm Alan, Jake's divorced father.

16:27.791 --> 16:30.885
- Keisha, Celeste's mother.
- Her mother?

16:31.061 --> 16:33.962
- Oh, please. You look like her sister.
- You're sweet.

16:34.131 --> 16:35.621
And single.

16:35.799 --> 16:37.266
Where's Jake?

16:38.035 --> 16:41.937
- Uh. Um, uh, uh, the...
- Actually...

16:42.106 --> 16:46.133
...he's, uh, distributing corn dogs
to the homeless tonight.

16:47.478 --> 16:49.412
But we'll make sure he gets your gift.

16:49.580 --> 16:52.208
Thanks for stopping by.
Merry Christmas.

16:53.951 --> 16:56.977
- Jake?
- Oh, hi.

16:57.154 --> 16:58.451
Who's this?

16:59.289 --> 17:02.383
Um, I don't know.

17:04.762 --> 17:07.856
- Who's she?
- Uh, Uncle Charlie?

17:08.732 --> 17:10.996
I don't know what to tell you, pal.

17:11.702 --> 17:13.397
It happens.

17:14.138 --> 17:17.005
- You said you didn't have a girlfriend.
- He doesn't.

17:17.207 --> 17:20.176
- Would you like some eggnog?
- You've got to be kidding.

17:22.079 --> 17:24.912
- You want some pie?
- You are such a liar.

17:25.416 --> 17:27.441
Why all the yelling? What's going on?

17:27.618 --> 17:30.212
- Uncle Charlie just ruined my life.
- What?

17:30.387 --> 17:34.289
He said it was okay to see other girls
as long as my girlfriend wasn't around.

17:34.458 --> 17:39.088
- Really? Is that what you believe?
- No, no, no. Not at all.

17:39.263 --> 17:42.562
He completely misunderstood me.
Merry Christmas.

17:43.801 --> 17:45.735
Yeah, right.

17:45.903 --> 17:47.803
Nice going.

17:51.508 --> 17:53.100
Would you like a lick?

17:54.278 --> 17:56.439
Not of that.

18:09.893 --> 18:13.795
- You wanna take your hand off my leg?
- I certainly do not.

18:22.306 --> 18:23.603
Love you.

18:23.774 --> 18:26.504
Yeah? Who do you love
when I'm not around?

18:28.345 --> 18:31.906
Hey, Uncle Charlie,
you really suck, you know that?

18:32.082 --> 18:34.277
Yeah, I've been told.

18:34.985 --> 18:40.013
Listen, Jake, would it be creepy
for you if I called Celeste's mom?

18:40.724 --> 18:42.282
Are you insane?

18:43.827 --> 18:45.590
Think about it.

18:46.797 --> 18:49.925
Here you go, sweetie.
Bite-size. Easy to chew.

18:53.170 --> 18:54.660
Marty?

18:54.838 --> 18:56.635
God. Marty?

18:57.141 --> 19:00.542
Ha! Just messing with you, you vulture.

19:00.711 --> 19:03.509
She thinks she's gonna sell my house
when I'm dead.

19:03.680 --> 19:05.944
But I ain't going.

19:06.817 --> 19:11.049
Oops. Actually, I am going.

19:13.690 --> 19:16.158
Merry Christmas, everybody.
